CHAPTER.VERS:
For I would not, brothers, have you

          {+}
         ignorant, that our fathers were all under the cloud, and all passed through the sea;

Neither be

          {+}
         idolaters, as were some of them; as it is written, The people sat down to eat and drink, and rose up to play.

Neither murmur

          {+}
        , as some of them murmured, and perished by the destroyer.

No trial has taken you

          {+}
         but such as man can bear: but God is faithful, who will not allow you

          {+}
         to be tried above what you

          {+}
         are able; but will with the trial also make the way of escape, that you

          {+}
         may be able to endure it.

I speak as to wise men; you

          {+}
         judge what I say.

But [I say], that the things which they sacrifice, they sacrifice to demons, and not to God: and I don't want you

          {+}
         to be partners with demons.

You

          {+}
         can't drink the cup of the Lord, and the cup of demons: you

          {+}
         can't partake of the table of the Lord, and of the table of demons.

If one of those who do not believe bids you

          {+}
         [to a feast], and you

          {+}
         are disposed to go; whatever is set before you

          {+}
        , eat, asking no question for conscience' sake.

But if any man says to you

          {+}
        , This has been offered in sacrifice, don't eat, for his sake that showed it, and for conscience sake:

Whether therefore you

          {+}
         eat, or drink, or whatever you

          {+}
         do, do all to the glory of God.
